{"seq":4,"slug":"data-structures","title":"数据结构","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":10,"docCount":40,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures","rating":{"composite":4.24,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.6,"coverage":4.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.47,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":3.25}},"introMarkdown":"# 数据结构 简介\n\n数据结构是计算机科学的基石之一。它研究的是如何在计算机中高效地组织、存储和管理数据，以便程序能够快速地执行查询、插入、删除和更新等操作。可以说，任何一段有意义的程序背后，都离不开对数据结构的选择与运用。\n\n掌握数据结构之所以重要，是因为它直接决定了算法的效率。同样的问题，选用不同的数据结构，可能带来数量级上的性能差异。无论是日常开发中对集合、映射、队列的使用，还是面试中对树、图、哈希表的深入考察，数据结构都是绕不开的核心知识。\n\n本手册面向计算机科学专业的学生、准备技术面试的求职者，以及希望夯实基础的软件开发者。无论你是初学者还是有一定经验的工程师，都可以在这里找到适合自己深度的内容。\n\n全书共分为五个章节，建议按照顺序依次学习：\n\n第一章「基础」从复杂度分析和大 O 表示法入手，帮助你建立衡量算法效率的思维框架。这是后续所有章节的理论基础，务必优先掌握。\n\n第二章「线性结构」介绍数组、链表、栈和队列这四种最经典的线性数据结构。它们是绝大多数高级数据结构的构建基石，理解它们的内存布局与操作特性至关重要。\n\n第三章「哈希与字符串」聚焦于哈希表的设计原理与字符串匹配算法。哈希表是实际工程中使用频率最高的数据结构之一，而字符串处理则是算法面试中的常见主题。\n\n第四章「树」涵盖二叉树、二叉搜索树、平衡树、堆和字典树等层次型结构。树形结构在数据库索引、操作系统调度、文本补全等场景中有着广泛的应用。\n\n第五章「图」探讨图的基本概念、最短路径、最小生成树和拓扑排序等核心问题。图是描述复杂关系的最通用模型，在网络路由、社交网络分析、任务调度等领域不可或缺。\n\n建议你在阅读每一章时，先理解概念与原理，再结合具体实现加以巩固。循序渐进地完成这五个章节，你将建立起完整而扎实的数据结构知识体系。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"fundamentals","title":"基础","docCount":2,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/fundamentals","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"complexity-analysis","title":"算法复杂度分析","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/fundamentals/complexity-analysis"},{"seq":2,"slug":"big-o-notation","title":"大O表示法","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/fundamentals/big-o-notation"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"linear-structures","title":"线性结构","docCount":4,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/linear-structures","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"arrays","title":"数组与动态数组","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/linear-structures/arrays"},{"seq":2,"slug":"linked-lists","title":"链表","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/linear-structures/linked-lists"},{"seq":3,"slug":"stacks","title":"栈","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/linear-structures/stacks"},{"seq":4,"slug":"queues","title":"队列与双端队列","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/linear-structures/queues"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"hash-and-strings","title":"哈希与字符串","docCount":2,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/hash-and-strings","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"hash-tables","title":"哈希表","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/hash-and-strings/hash-tables"},{"seq":2,"slug":"string-matching","title":"字符串匹配算法","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/hash-and-strings/string-matching"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"trees","title":"树","docCount":5,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/trees","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"binary-trees","title":"二叉树基础","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/trees/binary-trees"},{"seq":2,"slug":"binary-search-trees","title":"二叉搜索树","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/trees/binary-search-trees"},{"seq":3,"slug":"balanced-trees","title":"平衡树","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/trees/balanced-trees"},{"seq":4,"slug":"heaps","title":"堆与优先队列","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/trees/heaps"},{"seq":5,"slug":"tries","title":"字典树 Trie","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/trees/tries"}]},{"seq":5,"slug":"graphs","title":"图","docCount":4,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/graphs","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"graph-basics","title":"图的表示与遍历","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/graphs/graph-basics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"shortest-paths","title":"最短路径算法","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/graphs/shortest-paths"},{"seq":3,"slug":"minimum-spanning-trees","title":"最小生成树","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/graphs/minimum-spanning-trees"},{"seq":4,"slug":"topological-sort","title":"拓扑排序","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/graphs/topological-sort"}]},{"seq":6,"slug":"advanced-data-structures","title":"高级数据结构","docCount":4,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/data-structures/advanced-data-structures","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"union-find","tit